  "articleBody": "When you're tackling mobile home wall or ceiling repairs, it's easy to make a few common blunders that can cause more headaches later on. Here are some to watch out for: \n\n1. **Covering active leaks:** This is probably the biggest mistake. If there's water coming in, just patching over it won't solve anything; the problem will just reappear, often worse. Always fix the leak first and ensure the area is completely dry.\n\n2. **Ignoring rotted wood or sagging framing:** Damaged wall or ceiling material often hides structural issues. Skipping the step of inspecting and repairing any rotted wood or sagging framework means your fix won't last.\n\n3. **Skipping drying and vapor barriers:** After water damage, it's critical to let everything dry thoroughly and, if appropriate, reinstall vapor barriers. Rushing this can lead to mold or further material damage.\n\n4. **Failing to align replacement panels:** Mobile home panels need precise alignment and support. If they're not installed correctly, you'll end up with uneven surfaces and visible seams.\n\n5. **Not considering permits for major changes:** If your repair involves significant structural work or adding materials like drywall, you might need a permit. Always check local regulations to avoid issues.\n\nAvoiding these mistakes will help ensure your mobile home wall and ceiling repairs are done right and last.",
